    Bug 2064593 - Handle tray icon activation via keyboard. r=aleca

    In D306644, we upgraded the NOTIFYICONDATAW version to NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4, which changed the set of actions that trigger WM_LBUTTONDOWN. Per Microsoft (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/shellapi/nf-shellapi-shell_notifyicona):

    If a user selects a notify icon with the keyboard and activates it with the SPACEBAR or ENTER key, the version 5.0 Shell sends the associated application an NIN_KEYSELECT notification. Earlier versions send WM_RBUTTONDOWN [sic] and WM_RBUTTONUP [sic] messages.
    If a user selects a notify icon with the mouse and activates it with the ENTER key, the Shell now sends the associated application an NIN_SELECT notification. Earlier versions send WM_RBUTTONDOWN [sic] and WM_RBUTTONUP [sic] messages.

    In my experience, clicking the icon sends both WM_LBUTTONDOWN and NIN_SELECT, so let's handle the more abstract of the two so as to prevent HandleIconActivate from being called twice.

    Testing:
    1. Minimize Thunderbird
    2. Click the tray icon
    3. Thunderbird should reappear
    4. Minimze Thunderbird
    5. Select the tray icon with the tab key + arrows
    6. Press enter or space bar
    7. Thunderbird should reappear

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319731

